N2  - Angioneurotic oedema is a disorder, which is of importance in Otolaryngology given its propensity to cause airway obstruction. The diagnosis is made on clinical grounds in the acute setting. Further management can be guided by clinical presenting features which can be used to assess the risk of the patient going on to develop airway compromise. Management in the acute phase may require intubation or tracheostomy. Once the acute phase has been managed, follow up by an Otolaryngologist and an Immunologist can be arranged to allow confirmation of the diagnosis and initiation of prophylaxis against future attacks.
