TI  - Bradykinin in ACEI and other drug-induced angioedema
AU  - Brown, N.J.
PY  - 2025
PD  - 
N2  - Bradykinin induces vasodilation and vascular permeability by activating the B2 receptor and by stimulating release of the NK1 receptor agonist substance P. Bradykinin-mediated drug-induced angioedema results when drugs that decrease degradation of bradykinin [angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) and neprilysin inhibitors] or substance P [ACE, neprilysin, and dipeptidyl peptidase 4 (DPP4) inhibitors] or increase bradykinin production (tissue plasminogen activator, tPA) are administered to susceptible individuals. The risk of ACE inhibitor-associated angioedema is increased in patients of African descent, women, smokers, immunocompromised patients and those with seasonal allergies and decreased in patients with type 2 diabetes. Treatment consists of discontinuation of the offending drug. © 2025 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
