N2  - Allergy is a relevant issue for many individuals presenting with complex or unexplained breathlessness. A pathophysiological interaction between allergy and several common respiratory conditions is well recognised (e.g. allergic asthma), but it is less often considered that allergic-mediated sensitisation to environmental triggers can cause upper-airway inflammation and allied symptoms of rhinitis, leading to nasal occlusion and interplaying with conditions such as ILO. Other allergic conditions such as mast cell disorder may be overlooked. In this chapter, the assessment and management of common and relevant allergic conditions are described, and more uncommon conditions are discussed. © ERS 2021.
