N2  - BACKGROUND Iodophor (povidone-iodine) is widely used clinically because of its broad-spectrum antibacterial effects. Although extremely rare, it may cause anaphylactic shock, which itself carries the life-threatening risk of cardiac arrest. CASE SUMMARY We present a case in which a patient with postoperative infection went into anaphylactic shock and cardiac arrest caused by povidone-iodine during secondary surgery. The patient was successfully resuscitated by 2 h of cardiopul-monary resuscitation. CONCLUSION This is the first known case of cardiac arrest caused by povidone-iodine allergy © The Author(s) 2021. Published by Baishideng Publishing Group Inc. All rights reserved.
