TI  - Nonvisual Techniques of Tracheal Intubation
AU  - Poole, O.J.
AU  - Sparrow, K.
AU  - Hung, O.
PY  - 2022
PD  - 
N2  - While direct laryngoscopic intubation has been shown to be an effective and safe technique for many decades, it has some limitations, especially in the presence of specific anatomic variations. Many successful alternative intubation devices, including flexible endoscopes and video laryngoscopes, have been introduced during the last several decades. Unfortunately, these devices are substantially more expensive and visualization of the glottis may not be possible, particularly in a timely manner during emergency situations in the presence of fogging, blood, secretions, and vomitus. It is precisely these kinds of difficulties that have motivated the development of nonvisual techniques, which have proven to be simple, effective, and safe. Digital intubation, blind nasal intubation, and retrograde intubation are discussed in this chapter. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
