TI  - Airway management and acute airway obstruction
AU  - Choi, G.Y.S.
AU  - Joynt, G.M.
PY  - 2025
PD  - 
N2  - Obstruction of the airway is a life-threatening emergency. Causes of obstruction are many and varied. The rapid assessment followed by the immediate establishment of a patent airway is vital. No single management modality is universally applicable, and therefore the intensivist must be capable of performing a variety of airway management techniques. Non-invasive techniques appear simple, but require manual dexterity and regular practice to guarantee competence. While traditional rigid laryngoscopy remains a gold standard for tracheal intubation, video laryngoscopic techniques are increasingly available and may offer advantages in specific patients and situations. Alternative methods of securing an airway include flexible fibreoptic tracheal intubation, the use of a laryngeal mask, and the execution of a surgical airway, such as cricothyroidotomy or tracheostomy. Upper airway obstruction is uncommon, but immediately life threatening. Participation in airway courses and simulations to improve and maintain diagnostic and interventional skills in this setting is recommended. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved..
